Create the Cython output directory before CMake runs Cython into it.

CoolProp's Python wrapper is built by scikit-build-core driving the
CMakeLists under `wrappers/Python`. Two `add_custom_command`s cythonize the
wrapper sources with an explicit output path inside the build tree:

    ${Python_EXECUTABLE} -m cython ... \
        -o "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/CoolProp/CoolProp.cpp" ...

Cython does not create the parent directory of `-o`; it opens the file
directly, so if `CoolProp/` is not already there the build stops with
`[Errno 2] No such file or directory: .../CoolProp/CoolProp.cpp` (checked
against Cython 3.2.9). Whether the directory exists comes down to the
generator: Ninja creates each edge's output directories before running the
command, plain Makefiles do not — and this recipe asks only for `cmake` in
requirements.build, unlike the other scikit-build-core recipes in this tree,
which also pull `ninja`. A `file(MAKE_DIRECTORY ...)` at configure time makes
the build independent of that. One call covers both custom commands, since
`CoolProp.cpp` and `_constants.cpp` are written to the same directory.

The patch came in with the recipe (PR #49, squashed into ec8d184) and that PR
has an empty body, so the generator explanation above is read off the diff and
upstream's CMakeLists rather than from a recorded diagnosis; the patch's own
inline comment is the only rationale the tree preserves.

--- a/wrappers/Python/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/wrappers/Python/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -137,6 +137,9 @@ set(CYTHON_FLAGS
     --directive c_string_encoding=ascii
 )

+# Cython does not create the output's parent directory; create it ourselves.
+file(MAKE_DIRECTORY "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/CoolProp")
+
 # Generate CoolProp module
 add_custom_command(
     OUTPUT CoolProp/CoolProp.cpp
